---
// Be Secure's own widget (be-secure-receptionist.fly.dev — the same infrastructure
// that runs their phone system). It renders a card of recent completed jobs from
// a public, CORS-open feed carrying city, state, service and date only.
//
// The two lines below are the client's snippet, verbatim: `is:inline` keeps Astro
// from touching the script tag, so what ships is exactly what they asked for.
//
// The widget reserves 260px of height itself before it fetches, so it does not
// shift the page. It emits no structured data — schema stays the site's job.
---

<section>
  <div id="bsl-recent-jobs"></div>
  <script src="https://be-secure-receptionist.fly.dev/jobs-widget.js" async is:inline></script>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    max-width: 1360px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px 56px;
  }
  /* The widget's inline min-height stays put if its fetch fails (its catch is
     silent), which would leave a blank 260px hole. Collapse it while empty. */
  #bsl-recent-jobs:empty {
    min-height: 0 !important;
  }
</style>
